@amabukishuzo_official Yamahai Junmai Omachi. One of my favorite breweries known for utilizing yeast derived from flowers to give the sake a unique profile that is profound and elegant. 

This particular sake uses yeast derived from the marigold flower and Omachi rice. This gives it a particularly elegant floral nose and taste. It is amplified by the Yamahai Jikomi brewing process that allows lactic acid to naturally occur as opposed to adding it. This gives a slight funkiness similar to a natural wine. One of few in the line to be recommended to enjoy slightly warmed. When warmed, the floral notes become more announced, however when chilled, fruit forward sweetness comes out.

Want to see more? Follow this page for more sake introductions, or join us in our next sake tasting 3/23 @littlefishphilly. Link in the bio.
